  "facts": [
    "2nd gen: a user's write (REST and web SDK) carries authType app_user and authId the user's uid on every handler; admin and unauthenticated writes carry authType unknown",
    "1st gen: a user's write carries authType USER and context.auth with the uid and the token claims; admin writes carry ADMIN with no auth",
    "an ancestor write that creates or deletes children, an ancestor write one level down and a multi-path update each deliver one event per changed matching leaf and none for an unchanged leaf",
    "a handler that fails gets redelivered only when it has the retry flag: v2 retry:true and v1 failurePolicy; the retry-off v2 handler is not redelivered; the retry-on handlers needed up to 4 failures",
    "events keep their event id across redeliveries; the attempt pattern is compared by shape, not by count or timing"
  ],
  "scope": "69 compared rows of 12 writes over 3 handlers on the nested pattern /g9-rtdb/{group}/items/{id}, one instance, one region. The strict profile matches production in all 69 rows, attempt patterns by shape; the emulator profile's event shape is the declared difference /knownDifferences/triggerEventShapeEmulatorProfile, recorded against the official emulator's shape in CV14; no run of this recording compares firebase-tools. Not compared: delivery latency, retry timing and the order of deliveries across handlers."
